# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# Updates of tunable parameters (D[python-tunable]) on the GPU in double
# precision: an update during a run equals, to the bit, a compile with the
# new values from the same state (velocity Verlet, NVE, deterministic); an
# update and its inverse; the model without tunables; refused updates; the
# versions in the history, the states, and the energy file.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_tunable.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide updates GPU Double %t | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: GPU Double: the forces and energies of an update at step 8 equal those of a compile with the new values at that state to the bit
# CHECK: GPU Double: there and back
# CHECK: GPU Double: against the model without tunables
# CHECK: GPU Double: 6 refused updates change neither values nor version
# CHECK: GPU Double: versions [(0, 0), (5, 0), (10, 0), (15, 1), (20, 2)] in the energy file
# CHECK: updates passed
